# The repair probe waits for every member of each asked configuration
# instead of a Phase-1 quorum of qualifying answers: one member down for
# good blocks a lost slot that a quorum could decide. The audit's
# `blocked_in_asked` asks for a quorum, so it must not excuse the journal.
# Red on 3 of 600 seeds, never where the excuse fired (#773 (six
# excuse mutants survive)): convergence oracles catch it elsewhere.
# With #845 (fix-main)'s parked-replica fix it survived the same 600 seeds:
# a verdict on 3 seeds moves with the draws, so either is expected.
# Measured again for #1003 (uncounted skips from fix-main) on e10ad3a: it
# survived seeds 1..=600 while "loss: blocked in asked" fired on 96 runs.
# The mutant bites only when a lost slot's repair probe hears a faulty
# report and a member of an asked configuration is down for good while a
# Phase-1 quorum still qualifies. A down member that comes back in the
# tail answers, and the mutant goes on. The state needs a wipe of a member
# that holds no copy of the lost slot in a configuration of five, which the
# wipe budget seldom allows (#773 owns it).
excuse: loss: blocked in asked
expect: either #773
file: crates/lib/paros-core/src/proposer.rs
--- find
        .all(|config| config.has_phase1_quorum(&qualifying))
--- replace
        .all(|config| config.members().iter().all(|m| qualifying.contains(m)))
--- end
